{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017sSWt4SWcR9vZ59ewTJb1J","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"silicon PBE lattice constant 5.47 Å benchmark Haas Tran Blaha\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Lattice strain at c-Si surfaces: a density functional theory calculation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1412.3301\"},{\"title\":\"calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal 47and4fs7z\",\"url\":\"https://typeset.io/pdf/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-47and4fs7z.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals\",\"url\":\"https://www.bohrium.com/paper-details/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals/811872347643445248-529\"},{\"title\":\"suppl mater NJP108118 R1\",\"url\":\"https://pure.mpg.de/pubman/item/item_2599505_6/component/file_2618826/suppl-mater-NJP108118-R1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dissemin is shutting down on January 1st, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dissem.in/p/27732682/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals\"},{\"title\":\"docs.quantumatk.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.quantumatk.com/tutorials/silicon/silicon.html\"},{\"title\":\"nih.gov\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3331871\"},{\"title\":\"PBE0 calculations for bulk silicon\",\"url\":\"https://gpaw.readthedocs.io/tutorialsexercises/electronic/pbe0/pbe0.html\"},{\"title\":\"PBE0 calculations for bulk silicon¶\",\"url\":\"https://databases.fysik.dtu.dk/gpaw/tutorialsexercises/electronic/pbe0/pbe0.html\"},{\"title\":\"nih.gov\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3280356\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the Haas, Tran, and Blaha paper but not its silicon-specific PBE number, so the 5.47 Å figure is only indirectly supported.\n\n- **The benchmark paper:** Haas, Tran, and Blaha, \"Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals,\" DOI 10.1103/physrevb.79.085104. It assessed LDA, several GGAs including PBE, and TPSS on a set of 60 cubic solids. The performances of the LDA, GGA (PBE, AM05, WC, PBEsol, and SOGGA), and TPSS functionals for the lattice constants and bulk moduli were assessed on a set of 60 cubic solids. Its summary notes that for Al, most functionals except PBE yield accurate lattice constants. I did not find its silicon entry in the results.\n- **Silicon PBE values in other work:** A separate c-Si study reports PBE lattice constants of about 546.1 to 546.6 pm depending on pseudopotential and method, against an experimental value it uses for comparison. Those values match your 5.47 Å figure to within about 0.01 Å. The same study notes that a 4×4×4 k-point mesh and a plane-waves kinetic energy cutoff of 35 Rydberg gave a fully converged value.\n- **Experimental reference:** A QuantumATK tutorial uses 5.431 Angstrom as the experimental silicon lattice constant. It also notes that the bare PBE functional (without any pseudopotential projector shifts) is known to overestimate lattice constants in general, but for silicon only by 0.6%.\n\nTo confirm the exact 5.47 Å value against Haas et al., the paper's Table I would need to be checked directly, since the search did not return it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb97caf1-359b-4d6e-b946-6bba66471016","uuid":"1cd8bef3-0791-460e-90e0-964b115e668f","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:55:58.247Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"silicon PBE lattice constant 5.47 Å benchmark Haas Tran Blaha","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TZRN4xmr5eSXaDqEXMb9QP","content":[{"title":"Lattice strain at c-Si surfaces: a density functional theory calculation","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1412.3301"},{"title":"calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal 47and4fs7z","url":"https://typeset.io/pdf/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-47and4fs7z.pdf"},{"title":"Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals","url":"https://www.bohrium.com/paper-details/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals/811872347643445248-529"},{"title":"suppl mater NJP108118 R1","url":"https://pure.mpg.de/pubman/item/item_2599505_6/component/file_2618826/suppl-mater-NJP108118-R1.pdf"},{"title":"Dissemin is shutting down on January 1st, 2025","url":"https://dissem.in/p/27732682/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals"},{"title":"docs.quantumatk.com","url":"https://docs.quantumatk.com/tutorials/silicon/silicon.html"},{"title":"nih.gov","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3331871"},{"title":"PBE0 calculations for bulk silicon","url":"https://gpaw.readthedocs.io/tutorialsexercises/electronic/pbe0/pbe0.html"},{"title":"PBE0 calculations for bulk silicon¶","url":"https://databases.fysik.dtu.dk/gpaw/tutorialsexercises/electronic/pbe0/pbe0.html"},{"title":"nih.gov","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3280356"}]},"The search turned up the Haas, Tran, and Blaha paper but not its silicon-specific PBE number, so the 5.47 Å figure is only indirectly supported.\n\n- **The benchmark paper:** Haas, Tran, and Blaha, \"Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals,\" DOI 10.1103/physrevb.79.085104. It assessed LDA, several GGAs including PBE, and TPSS on a set of 60 cubic solids. The performances of the LDA, GGA (PBE, AM05, WC, PBEsol, and SOGGA), and TPSS functionals for the lattice constants and bulk moduli were assessed on a set of 60 cubic solids. Its summary notes that for Al, most functionals except PBE yield accurate lattice constants. I did not find its silicon entry in the results.\n- **Silicon PBE values in other work:** A separate c-Si study reports PBE lattice constants of about 546.1 to 546.6 pm depending on pseudopotential and method, against an experimental value it uses for comparison. Those values match your 5.47 Å figure to within about 0.01 Å. The same study notes that a 4×4×4 k-point mesh and a plane-waves kinetic energy cutoff of 35 Rydberg gave a fully converged value.\n- **Experimental reference:** A QuantumATK tutorial uses 5.431 Angstrom as the experimental silicon lattice constant. It also notes that the bare PBE functional (without any pseudopotential projector shifts) is known to overestimate lattice constants in general, but for silicon only by 0.6%.\n\nTo confirm the exact 5.47 Å value against Haas et al., the paper's Table I would need to be checked directly, since the search did not return it."],"durationSeconds":5.254283915999993,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017sSWt4SWcR9vZ59ewTJb1J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
