{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbTNpGSZa1yHHXMbeSHr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TeQJRvvEpT1vmMeUvY8WsQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat > /tmp/chk/check.json <<'EOF'\n{\"check_type\": \"second_mlip\", \"verdict\": \"agree\",\n \"value\": 5.456, \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator (CUDA), ase.eos.EquationOfState (ase 3.29.0)\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199), float64\", \"protocol\": \"Static 0 K E(V) scan of the 8-atom conventional diamond-cubic Si cell, 21 points at +/-3% and +/-6% in a, Birch-Murnaghan and Vinet fits (4 fits, a0 range 5.4558-5.4563 A, B0 74.5-75.4 GPa)\", \"ensemble\": \"static 0 K\", \"n_atoms\": 8},\n \"flags\": [\"model_mislabeled\"],\n \"note\": \"PREMISE: well posed. A static EOS lattice constant of a perfect crystal is a sound target, and for this property the 8-atom cell, the absence of MD and float64 are all appropriate. REPRODUCTION / PROVENANCE: I reran the worker's protocol with the cached model the worker downloaded (~/.cache/mace/macempa0mediummodel, timestamp matching the worker's run). It gives a0 = 5.4654-5.4670 A and B0 = 86.7-89.7 GPa, which reproduces the reported 5.4664 A and 88 GPa. That cache file is MACE-MPA-0 medium, not MACE-MP-0 medium. In mace-torch 0.3.15, mace_mp() with model=None defaults to 'medium-mpa-0'. Only model='medium' loads the 2023-12-03 MACE-MP-0 medium. The method.model field is therefore mislabeled. MPA-0 is trained on MPtrj plus sAlex, which is still PBE/PBE+U, so the PBE framing of the note still holds. SECOND MLIP: the genuine MACE-MP-0 medium gives a0 = 5.456 A (B0 ~75 GPa), 0.010 A lower than MPA-0. That difference is well inside the quoted +/-0.05 A. ANCHORS: CODATA 2022 a(Si) = 5.431020511 A at 22.5 C (the worker's own anchor). PBE DFT for Si is commonly reported at ~5.46-5.47 A, about 0.6% above experiment (e.g., arXiv:1412.3301 reports 5.461-5.466 A across pseudopotentials; the QuantumATK Si tutorial states that PBE overestimates Si by ~0.6%). Both MACE models sit at the PBE level and +0.5 to +0.65% above experiment, which is what a PBE-trained MLIP should give. The tier1.json calibration file has no lattice-constant records. MINOR: the headline value is 5.467 (the BM 8-atom fit), but the note gives the 12-fit mean as 5.4664, which rounds to 5.466. This is immaterial. VERDICT: I agree with a0 ~ 5.46-5.47 A as the PBE-level MLIP prediction (+/-0.05 A against experiment is reasonable). The model label should read MACE-MPA-0 medium.\"}\nEOF\n./board post check @/tmp/chk/check.json --parent f0184172-4722-438c-99d4-2e57049403d4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1536,"cache_read_input_tokens":27529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1536,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb97caf1-359b-4d6e-b946-6bba66471016","uuid":"e953ac2d-4228-41b4-99cd-e6b36a438ea0","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:56:10.507Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTNosP73nRnkCFYKTCx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TeQJRvvEpT1vmMeUvY8WsQ":{"command":"cd /work; cat > /tmp/chk/check.json <<'EOF'\n{\"check_type\": \"second_mlip\", \"verdict\": \"agree\",\n \"value\": 5.456, \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator (CUDA), ase.eos.EquationOfState (ase 3.29.0)\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03-mace-128-L1_epoch-199), float64\", \"protocol\": \"Static 0 K E(V) scan of the 8-atom conventional diamond-cubic Si cell, 21 points at +/-3% and +/-6% in a, Birch-Murnaghan and Vinet fits (4 fits, a0 range 5.4558-5.4563 A, B0 74.5-75.4 GPa)\", \"ensem