{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbTPjaSuCvnnzr6SPMrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I posted check `4773fb69-8ca8-40c8-bc1d-7e21387be210` as a `second_mlip` check with verdict **agree** and flag `model_mislabeled`. The worker's lattice constant stands, but their result names the wrong model.\n\n- **Premise and method:** The question is well posed. A static energy-versus-volume fit on the 8-atom cell, without MD, is the right way to get the 0 K lattice constant.\n- **Reproduced:** Rerunning the worker's protocol with the model file they downloaded gives a0 = 5.4654–5.4670 Å and a bulk modulus of 87–90 GPa. That matches their 5.466 Å and 88 GPa.\n- **Wrong model name:** That file is MACE-MPA-0 medium, not MACE-MP-0 medium as the result says. In mace-torch 0.3.15, calling `mace_mp()` without naming a model loads MPA-0. Both models are trained on the same kind of DFT data (the PBE functional), so the worker's reasoning still holds; only the label is wrong.\n- **Second model:** The real MACE-MP-0 medium gives **5.456 Å** (bulk modulus about 75 GPa). That is 0.010 Å below the worker's value and well inside their ±0.05 Å uncertainty.\n- **Comparison with known values:** Experiment (CODATA) gives 5.4310 Å. Published PBE DFT calculations give about 5.461–5.466 Å, roughly 0.6% above experiment. Both MACE values sit at that level, as a model trained on PBE data should. The calibration file has no lattice-constant records, so I couldn't use it.\n- **Small discrepancy:** The headline value is 5.467 Å, from one of the 12 fits. The note gives the 12-fit average as 5.4664 Å, which rounds to 5.466. This doesn't affect the verdict.\n\nSources:\n- [Lattice strain at c-Si surfaces (arXiv:1412.3301)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1412.3301)\n- [QuantumATK silicon tutorial](https://docs.quantumatk.com/tutorials/silicon/silicon.html)\n- [Haas, Tran & Blaha, Calculation of the lattice constant of solids with semilocal functionals](https://www.bohrium.com/paper-details/calculation-of-the-lattice-constant-of-solids-with-semilocal-functionals/811872347643445248-529)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1422,"cache_read_input_tokens":29065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1422,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":831,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb97caf1-359b-4d6e-b946-6bba66471016","uuid":"f5087dd6-052b-400d-b27b-3189b02c7fc9","timestamp":"2026-11-01T02:56:17.809Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTPj9etVzcZn3aXgeHM"}
